// D16497 — float arithmetic over a value join of literals (`0.1 * (if c { 0.3 } else { 0.7 })`)
// delivered into an `f32` computes there, as the join alone does (ruling 4.3); the un-annotated
// face has no `f32` and computes at `f64`.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function __no(): boolean { return false }
// @@VALUE@@
0.1 * (if __no() { 0.3 } else { 0.7 })
// @@TYPE@@
f32
// @@PROOF@@
print(v)
// @@WANT@@
0.07000000029802322
// @@WANT_UNANNOTATED@@
0.06999999999999999
// @@SKIP@@
return_inferred: an inferred return is f64 before its f32 caller is seen, as for a bare 0.7
